[5.589299, "o", "# Workflow optimization task\r\n\r\nYou are optimizing this developer’s AI-assisted development workflow. Caliper — a local, evidence-driven analyzer — inspected their coding-agent sessions and configuration and produced the findings below. Apply the safe, high-value fixes, verify each one, and report what you changed.\r\n\r\n## Operating rules (read first)\r\n1. Make minimal, reversible changes. Back up any configuration file before editing it (e.g. copy it to `<file>.bak`).\r\n2. Never read, print, commit, or transmit secrets or credentials. If a fix involves a secret, move it to an environment variable and reference it — do not echo its value.\r\n3. Verify every change. After code edits, run the project’s test suite. If Caliper is installed, re-run `caliper audit` to confirm the findings are resolved.\r\n4. Use judgment. These findings are evidence-backed but observational, not experimentally proven. Skip anything that does not apply to this project, and prefer the least invasive fix.\r\n5. Never delete or weaken tests to make a check pass.\r\n6. Put durable workflow/instruction improvements in CLAUDE.md (project root, or global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md).\r\n7. Finish with a short changelog: what you changed, why, and how to roll each change back.\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n- Analysis generated: 2026-01-15 17:00 UTC · window: last 1d 8h\r\n- Agents detected: opencode, codex, claude\r\n"]
